<header><p class="enc-kicker">Religion / idea · deity</p><h1 class="enc-title">Jagannath</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Jagannath, Lord of the Universe, is a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hinduism">Hindu</a> deity worshipped as a form of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vishnu">Vishnu</a> or <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/krishna">Krishna</a>, chiefly at his temple in Puri, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/odisha">Odisha</a>, together with Balabhadra and Subhadra. The present temple was begun by the Eastern Ganga king <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anantavarman-chodaganga">Anantavarman Chodaganga</a> in the 12th century, and the kings of Odisha served as the god's first servants. His annual <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chariot">chariot</a> festival, the Rath Yatra, draws huge crowds.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/jagannath.jpg" alt="Jagannath" width="320" height="693" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: no bias — קיין אומוויסנדיקע פּרעפֿערענצן — keyn umvisndike preferentsn · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Rath_Yatra_in_Munich_2020,_Lord_Jagannath_20200725_160839.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
